course: dictionary
lesson: 3974
title: Gadget: a handy little machine
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gadget is a small, clever machine or tool that does a useful job. Context helps you work it out: «a handy gadget», «kitchen gadgets» and «the latest gadget» tell you it is a thing you use, often in the home.
explain: «Not everything people do is about you; a doorbell camera is a common gadget, not an insult.» The word common tells you that many people have gadgets. A doorbell camera is a thing you use, so gadget means a useful device, not a rude word.
explain: «A boy in England paid for an influencer's favourite gadget after a video; it was a paid advert, and the gadget broke in a week.» Paid and favourite tell you the gadget was something people buy. Broke in a week tells you it was not very strong. Swap in your meaning, "a small device that broke in a week", and it still makes sense.
fact: Gadget means a small, clever machine or tool that does a useful job.
fact: Informally, gadget can mean any small electronic device, like a phone or tablet.
fact: «Gadgets» is the plural: one gadget, two or more gadgets.
fact: «Kitchen gadgets» are tools such as can openers that help you cook.
fact: A good check is to swap in "machine or tool" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She bought the latest gadget for her kitchen.» What is a gadget here? | A kind of cake baked in a tin | A long walk in the rain | A quiet, gloomy sort of sad | *A small, clever machine or tool that does a useful job
exercise: «Not everything people do is about you; a doorbell camera is a common gadget, not an insult.» Which word tells you many people have gadgets? | *common | about | doorbell | insult
exercise: Ella asks, «Is a phone a gadget?» What is the answer? | No, gadgets are only for spies in stories | *Yes, informally, a phone is a small electronic device, so it can be called a gadget | No, a phone is a kind of animal | Yes, but only when it is broken
test: «A boy in England paid for an influencer's favourite gadget after a video.» What does gadget mean here? | A type of video | *A small device that people buy and use | A rude word | A holiday in England
test: In «the gadget broke in a week», which clue tells you the gadget was not very strong? | favourite | video | *broke in a week | paid for
exam: Which phrase means the same as «a handy gadget»? | a wet, grey day | a long, quiet walk | a loud, angry noise | *a useful little machine
